  "notes": [
    "Eligible stars are HVS 3, HVS 7, and HVS 15, the three targets in T:p2-b5; that passage places them in the prior HVS Survey's 21 unbound stars and says Han et al. (2025) identified the LMC-origin HVSs, so their unbound candidacy is follow-up rather than newly established here. Gaia DR3 is used for their source IDs because T:p9-b6 says the three-HVS constraints use Gaia DR3 proper motions. The 'HVS 5' in T:p3-b4 conflicts with the three-star sample and Table 1 (T:p2-b5, T:p3-b0); it is treated as a typo for HVS 15, not an additional star.",
    "HVS 3: Table 1 (T:p3-b0, mirrored by image I:p3-b0) lists HVS 3's RA and Dec without uncertainties; the distance, proper-motion components, and radial velocity include the reported errors. All quantities are the present-day initial conditions adopted for the orbit integrations. The reported ejection time of HVS 3 (19 ± 2 Myr ago; T:p4-b7) is not among the requested quantities. The LMC Center row of Table 1 is not the target star and was not extracted.",
    "HVS 7: Table 1 lists HVS 7's present-day phase-space initial conditions used in the orbit integrations. The paper also reports an inferred ejection time for HVS 7 of 219^{+27}_{-40} Myr ago, but ejection time is not among the requested quantities. No Galactocentric radius, total Galactic-rest-frame speed, or bound/unbound probabilities are reported individually for HVS 7.",
    "HVS 15: Table 1 identifies HVS 15 with Gaia source_id 3794074603484360704. The RA and Dec values are reported without uncertainties in Table 1."
  ]
}
